# Example: How to Implement a Page

Pages in this project are Vue single-file components located in the [pages/](mdc:pages) directory. For example, the login page is implemented in [pages/login/index.vue](mdc:pages/login/index.vue):

- Use `<script setup>` for logic and state
- Use `definePageMeta` to set page metadata, layout, and middleware
- Use Pinia stores for state management (e.g., user authentication)
- Use FormKit for form fields and validation
- Use composables and Nuxt utilities for API calls (e.g., `useFetch`)
- Use NuxtLink for navigation
- Organize the UI with Tailwind CSS classes

See the login page for a full example of these practices.
